From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:57:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(approval): retry a smart approval judge the provider
 could not serve

When a Claude account hit its weekly limit, the provenance review's own model call failed the same way and the card read "Smart approval could not decide (the review model call failed: ClaudeAPIError)". A judge call that fails for a provider limit (429, plan or usage limit, every pool account at its limit) or a transient error (timeout, overloaded, 5xx, connection) is now tried again before the user is asked: once more on the same route, where the claude-pool provider moves to its next account, then for stage 2 on the stage-1 route (smart_fast_model) with the stage-2 prompt. The retry's verdict is used. The same-route retry is skipped after a timeout (it already cost a whole window and call_llm's own retries) and when every pool account is at its limit. The fallback is skipped when the stage-1 route already failed in the same review, is the same model, or is self-hosted while stage 2 is hosted; a self-hosted fallback's allow gets the same 0086/0095 holds. No new config keys and no sleeps: at most two calls per route.

A judge failure never allows. When every route fails, the verdict stays unsure and the card says "Smart approval could not review this: the review model was unavailable (all Claude accounts are at their limit). Approve or deny it yourself.", with the pool's reset time when it has one. Other failures are not retried and keep asking, but the card no longer names the exception class ("Smart approval could not decide (the review model call failed)"); the log keeps it.
